Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: a packet whose time is in doubt anchors no disc
 time

The time shown for a disc pairs each packet's read time with its dts.
Where a disc jumps back in time - two clips joined without a seamless
connection, both starting at the same timestamp - the player is not
yet sure of the jump on the first packet past it, and takes its time
away until another stream confirms it. That packet then went in with
the dts of the packet before it and the read time of the new clip: an
anchor of the old clip's end giving the new clip's start, so for the
last moments the old clip played out the time shown fell to nothing.

A packet without a time of its own now adds no anchor.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
index d4046b68..51678587 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -2829,7 +2829,8 @@ void CVideoPlayer::UpdateTimestamps(CCurrentStream& current, DemuxPacket* pPacke
 
   current.dispTime = pPacket->dispTime;
 
-  if (m_pInputStream &&
+  // a packet whose time is still in doubt carries the last one, not its own: no anchor
+  if (m_pInputStream && (pPacket->dts != DVD_NOPTS_VALUE || pPacket->pts != DVD_NOPTS_VALUE) &&
       (&current == &m_CurrentVideo || (&current == &m_CurrentAudio && m_CurrentVideo.id < 0)))
   {
     if (CDVDInputStream::IDisplayTime* displayTime = m_pInputStream->GetIDisplayTime())
